{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And she sent her amah.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory differed — Rabbi Yehudah and Rabbi Nechemiah: one said 'her hand,' and one said 'her maidservant.' The one who said 'her hand' — her arm was extended sixty cubits. And there is an allusion in the verse, in that Pharaoh's daughter said, ״כי מן המים משיתיהו״ — for from the water I drew him: the nun and the two hehs are superfluous, for Scripture could have said ״כי ממים משיתיו״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:55:30.053882409Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}